@node Parenthesis highlighting
@section Parenthesis highlighting

@findex modus-themes-extras-highlight-parentheses
The function @code{modus-themes-extras-highlight-parentheses} configures the @samp{highlight-parentheses} package to use colors from the active Modus theme. It retrieves intense background colors (cyan@comma{} magenta@comma{} green@comma{} yellow) and their corresponding foreground colors from the Modus palette via @code{modus-themes-get-color-value} and sets @code{highlight-parentheses-background-colors} and @code{highlight-parentheses-colors} accordingly.

If @code{global-highlight-parentheses-mode} is available@comma{} the function also enables it. This function is suitable for use in the @code{modus-themes-after-load-theme-hook} or any theme-switching hook to keep parenthesis colors synchronized with the active theme.

@node Extra face customization
@section Extra face customization

@findex modus-themes-extras-set-faces
The function @code{modus-themes-extras-set-faces} is provided as a hook point for additional theme-specific face customizations. Its body is currently empty@comma{} but its docstring shows how to add conditional face settings based on the active theme:

@lisp
(if (eq modus-themes-extras-light-theme (car custom-enabled-themes))
    (set-face-attribute 'hl-sentence nil :background "#bfefff")
  (set-face-attribute 'hl-sentence nil :background "#004065"))
@end lisp

You can add such expressions to this function and call it from a theme-loading hook to apply per-theme face adjustments.

